The moon shines brighter than the sun.
"Welcome, my child," her voice echoes
Dizziness grips you.
Your body, no longer yours, refuses to move.
Thoughts slip away, leaving only a deep, resonating silence.
"You have proven yourself worthy," 
Your limbs begin to writhe and twist, as if they have a mind of their own.
"You will guard these waters," her voice fades with the wind.
You gasp for air, but the air gives no relief.
You find yourself at the water's edge.
"Back to sea with you, little one." she gently whispers.
The ocean's call, once daunting, now feels like destiny. 
As you slip beneath the waves, your new form takes shape. 